BITBUCKET PRACTICAL – FULL STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION
STEP 1: Create Repository on Bitbucket
1. Open https://bitbucket.org/
2. Login → Repositories → Create Repository
3. Give name: my-bitbucket-project
4. Click Create Repository
STEP 2: Clone Repository Locally
git clone https://bitbucket.org/your_username/my-bitbucket-project.git
cd my-bitbucket-project
STEP 3: Create a File
echo "This is Bitbucket test file" > example.txt
STEP 4: Add File to Staging Area
git add example.txt
STEP 5: Commit File
git commit -m "Added example.txt with sample content"
STEP 6: Create New Branch
git checkout -b feature
STEP 7: Modify File in Feature Branch
echo "More content added in feature branch" >> example.txt
git add example.txt
git commit -m "Updated example.txt in feature branch"
STEP 8: Push Feature Branch to Bitbucket
git push -u origin feature
STEP 9: Create Pull Request on Bitbucket
1. Open Bitbucket website
2. Go to Pull Requests → Create Pull Request
3. Source: feature, Target: main
4. Click Merge
STEP 10: Show Commit History
git log --oneline
